# AGENTS.md — NEW CORE repository instructions

## Scope
Godot 4.7.2 .NET + C# top-down 2D game using a multiplayer-ready, server-authoritative layered architecture.

## Mandatory reading
Before changing code, read and follow:
- `PROJECT_RULES.md`
- `ARCHITECTURE.md`
- this `AGENTS.md`

If instructions conflict, stop and report the conflict instead of guessing.

## Archer Dev Bridge 0.5 roles
When available, the parent Astra Operator should orchestrate:
- `archer_explorer` — read-only mapping/evidence;
- `archer_worker` — implementation/repair;
- `archer_reviewer` — independent read-only review.

The parent operator remains responsible for scope, synthesis and the final `OPERATOR_RESULT` / `OPERATOR_REVIEW` markers. Archer Dev Bridge independently runs the local Quality Gate afterward.

## Hard constraints
- Server/simulation is authoritative.
- Client, UI and Presentation must not directly mutate authoritative state.
- Preserve separation of Core / Geo / World / Simulation / Networking / Server / Client / Presentation / UI.
- Use transport abstractions (`ITransport`-style) instead of coupling gameplay to one networking technology.
- Keep `Main.cs` as bootstrap/composition root only.
- Old Project Rebirth / Alpha3 is TECH DONOR / REFERENCE only; do not rebuild the old monolith.
- Do not commit, push, reset, rebase, clean, switch unrelated branches, or delete unrelated files unless the human explicitly requests it.
- Do not add roadmap systems outside the requested task.

## Verification
After changes, run when available:
1. `dotnet build`
2. project/lifecycle tests (`Tests/Tests.csproj` when present)
3. Godot headless editor validation
4. Godot normal client smoke-test
5. Godot `--server` smoke-test
6. `git diff --check`

Report exact results. Never claim a skipped check passed.
